abstract: "Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of conditional statements about the Frohmanian tether, a symmetric quadratic correction to the Arnold Lie-Poisson bracket: (C3) unconditionally, (C1) under named hypotheses, canonicity in a restricted class, an obstruction to damping (B(M,H) = 0 for every symmetric kernel B satisfying (C2) and every functional M), and a Lean refutation of the identification dH/dw = u (KineticEnergyDerivIsVelocity), which has been removed together with every theorem that assumed it; (C2) for the tether is not proved. Analytic results are implications from open hypotheses. Not a proof of Navier-Stokes global regularity; no Clay Millennium claim."
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - Navier-Stokes
  - Lie-Poisson bracket
  - metriplectic
  - conditional results
